{% comment %}
  Variant (flavour) swatches for the product buy box.

  By default one swatch per variant, which is right for a product whose only
  option is the flavour. Name a product option in the block instead and the row
  collapses to that option's values — so a product built as Flavour × Supply
  shows four flavours rather than every combination of the two.

  Each swatch still carries a single variant id, because that is what the script
  and the cart want. For a named option the id is that value's first available
  variant, falling back to its first variant when the whole value is sold out.

  Renders nothing when there is only one thing to choose, so the block can be
  left in place on products that do not need it.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the flavors block. Reads settings.label and
    settings.option_name.
  - product {Object} - product whose variants are shown.
  - current_variant {Object} - variant currently selected.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-flavors__block', block: block, product: hero_product, current_variant: current_variant %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign wanted_option = block.settings.option_name | strip | downcase
  assign option_position = 0

  if wanted_option != blank
    for product_option in product.options_with_values
      assign this_name = product_option.name | strip | downcase
      if this_name == wanted_option
        assign option_position = product_option.position
        assign option_values = product_option.values
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Both modes reduce to "group the variants by some property and show one
    swatch per distinct value of it" — the option name for a named option, the
    variant title otherwise. Naming that property once is what lets a single
    loop below serve both, and it keeps the no-option path rendering exactly
    what it rendered before: one swatch per variant.

    A name that matches no option on the product falls through to that same
    default rather than printing an empty row, so a typo degrades to the old
    behaviour instead of losing the picker.
  endcomment
  if option_position > 0
    assign match_key = 'option' | append: option_position
    assign swatch_values = option_values
  else
    assign match_key = 'title'
    assign swatch_values = product.variants | map: 'title'
  endif
-%}

{%- if swatch_values.size > 1 -%}
  <div {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {% if block.settings.label != blank %}
      <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__label">{{ block.settings.label }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <div
      class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavors"
      {% if option_position > 0 %}
        data-cwc-flavor-position="{{ option_position }}"
      {% endif %}
    >
      {%- for swatch_value in swatch_values -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign matches = product.variants | where: match_key, swatch_value
          assign in_stock = matches | where: 'available', true
          assign swatch_variant = in_stock.first | default: matches.first
        -%}

        {%- if swatch_variant != blank -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor{% if current_variant[match_key] == swatch_value %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor--selected{% endif %}{% if in_stock.size == 0 %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor--unavailable{% endif %}"
            data-cwc-variant="{{ swatch_variant.id }}"
            {% if option_position > 0 %}
              data-cwc-flavor-value="{{ swatch_value | escape }}"
            {% endif %}
            {% if in_stock.size == 0 %}
              disabled
            {% endif %}
          >
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-swatch{% if swatch_variant.image == blank %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-swatch--empty{% endif %}">
              {% if swatch_variant.image != blank %}
                <img
                  src="{{ swatch_variant.image | image_url: width: 100 }}"
                  alt="{{ swatch_value | escape }}"
                  width="100"
                  height="100"
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              {% else %}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-empty-label">Image</span>
              {% endif %}
            </span>
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-name">{{ swatch_value }}</span>
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
